      "message": "The compile_ffmpeg_deps_windows.sh attached to https://issues.webmproject.org/issues/355182136 shows that the bug reporter downloaded https://github.com/yasm/yasm/releases/download/v1.3.0/yasm-1.3.0-win64.exe\n\nThis file depends on the following two DLLS:\n\n```\nC:\\Users\\wtc\\Downloads\u003edumpbin /dependents yasm-1.3.0-win64.exe\nMicrosoft (R) COFF/PE Dumper Version 14.42.34435.0\nCopyright (C) Microsoft Corporation.  All rights reserved.\n\n\nDump of file yasm-1.3.0-win64.exe\n\nFile Type: EXECUTABLE IMAGE\n\n  Image has the following dependencies:\n\n    MSVCR100.dll\n    KERNEL32.dll\n\n  Summary\n\n       15000 .data\n        6000 .pdata\n       37000 .rdata\n        6000 .reloc\n        1000 .rsrc\n       53000 .text\n\n```\n\nSo the problem is that MSVCR100.dll is missing. It is a redistributable of Visual C++ 2010.\n\nSo we should clarify two things.\n\n1. \"yasm.torball.net 1.3.0 binaries\" should be changed to https://github.com/yasm/yasm/releases/download/v1.3.0/yasm-1.3.0-win64.exe\n\n2. Instead of \"issues with VS2022 and GitHub actions\", say \"missing Visual C++ 2010 redistributable\" or \"missing MSVCR100.dll\".",
